  "items": [
    {
      "headline": "Mexico aviation authority faces FAA safety evaluation",
      "context": "The Mexican civil aviation authority will undergo US FAA assessment this week on safety standards compliance, with potential consequences for Mexico's aviation category ranking.",
      "background": "The FAA restored Mexico to Category 1 in September 2023. This review tests whether Mexico's aviation authority still meets international safety-oversight standards. Mexico is not currently trying to regain the rating.",
      "view": "The risk is a future downgrade, not a current Category 2 restriction. Category 1 lets Mexican airlines add US routes and codeshares, so the useful question is whether the authority has maintained staffing, rules and oversight since the 2023 restoration.",
      "prediction": "Watch the FAA's country-rating list and any formal notice after the review. Category 1 staying in place would confirm continued compliance. A downgrade would again limit new US routes and codeshares.",
      "analysisV": 9,
      "analysisRefs": {
