      "headline": "Mexico's Treasury reforms governmental accounting manual",
      "context": "Official gazette publication of reforms to Mexico's Manual de Contabilidad Gubernamental establishes new accounting and reporting standards for federal entities.",
      "background": "Mexico's national accounting council sets a common rulebook for federal, state and municipal public accounts. The official gazette published changes to both the manual and its conceptual framework.",
      "view": "The reform changes how public entities record and report money, not how much they can spend. Its value depends on whether the new statements make obligations and transfers easier to compare across entities, including federal support for Pemex.",
      "prediction": "Watch whether the next quarterly financial statements use the new classifications consistently. Common treatment would show adoption, while different treatment across entities would reveal an implementation gap.",
