      "headline": "AT&T and Telcel may be barred from intelligent networks spectrum auction due to spectrum concentration",
      "context": "Mexico's communications regulator has proposed excluding carriers holding more than 20 percent of spectrum in PCS, AWS, 2.3 GHz, 2.5 GHz, 3.3 GHz, and 3.5 GHz bands from accumulating additional spectrum in the intelligent networks auction.",
      "background": "The regulator's public consultation ended in July, so the 20% cap is still part of draft auction rules, not a completed award. The trade agreement calls for transparent spectrum procedures that promote competition.",
